        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088583
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T21:07:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e when an agent does forget --cbr or --yes, it still hangs in vi or on stdin until timeout. the goal is to never hang headless tools\n\nthis feels like scope creep compared to addressing https://crbug.com/gerrit/553024110. proper headless execution shouldn\u0027t rely on detecting proprietary/internal envvars, it should rely on standard streams and intentional, generic flags like `-y`\n\nrepo already checks for headless environments by checking `isatty` natively:\nhttps://cs.opensource.google/gerrit/gerrit/git-repo/+/main:hooks.py;l\u003d216-217;drc\u003de6ad7080098a0db0cb304812c8603856da2bebf2\n\nif a headless tool (agent or not) forgets to pass `--yes` or `--cbr`, fixing the caller is the right approach, rather than modifying repo to guess the intent",
      "parentUuid": "f86205ce_d19d6f3a",
